Please try again.
Split amounts must equal ₹2,500.

Do not expose raw SwiftData or system errors to users.

Use typed errors where practical.

29. Swift Coding Standards

Follow modern Swift conventions.

Prefer:

struct for value types
enum for finite states
final class when reference semantics are required
private wherever possible
let instead of var when values do not change
Small focused methods
Strong typing
Codable where appropriate
async/await for asynchronous operations

Avoid:

Unnecessary force unwraps
Massive ViewModels
Massive Views
Global mutable state
Hardcoded strings
Business logic inside View bodies
30. SwiftUI State Management

Use appropriate state management.

Use:

@State

for local View state.

Use:

@Binding

for values owned by a parent.

Use the project's chosen Swift observation approach for ViewModels.

Avoid global singleton state for normal application data.

31. Dependency Injection

